  "body": "This is rather a Chrome/ium implementation question than an issue with the specification. Since Chrome/ium is the only browser so far supporting the WebUSB API I think it's still an appropriate place to discuss this issue.\r\n\r\nDevice enumeration is a sensitive operation. According to the specification the browser / UA needs to know at all times which USB devices are connected to the host. I couldn't find any details in which process the device enumeration happens. I know that the permission API runs in the main process and is therefore protected from a compromised renderer process, i.e., once the renderer process is compromised through a code execution vulnerability one could not just give permissions to every connected USB device. How about the device enumeration itself? Does this happen in the main browser process as well or are there similar protections against a compromised renderer process?",
